WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.968
-Thank you, thank you,
thank you.

00:00:01.968 --> 00:00:03.036
I'm so happy that you're here.

00:00:03.036 --> 00:00:05.638
-Me too. Very exciting.
-I'm a fan.

00:00:05.638 --> 00:00:07.239
It's your first time
on our show.

00:00:07.239 --> 00:00:09.942
-Yes.
-I want to get to know you.

00:00:09.942 --> 00:00:12.278
I want to ask you -- you're
from Cuba, is that correct?

00:00:12.278 --> 00:00:14.614
-Yeah.
-And did you start acting there?

00:00:14.614 --> 00:00:15.749
-I did.

00:00:15.749 --> 00:00:18.517
I went to drama school
when I was 14.

00:00:18.517 --> 00:00:21.521
That was like, four years
of theater school.

00:00:21.521 --> 00:00:22.922
-Yeah.

00:00:22.922 --> 00:00:26.092
-And when I was on my second
year, I did my first movie.

00:00:26.092 --> 00:00:27.593
I auditioned for it
and I got it,

00:00:27.593 --> 00:00:30.596
and the teachers
were not very happy

00:00:30.596 --> 00:00:32.131
and they told me
if I did the movie,

00:00:32.131 --> 00:00:33.799
I was going to --
[ Clicks tongue ]

00:00:33.799 --> 00:00:35.901
get kicked out of school.
-Of acting school?

00:00:35.901 --> 00:00:37.437
-Yeah, because, you know...
-Wait.

00:00:37.437 --> 00:00:38.904
This is kind of the goal, right?

00:00:38.904 --> 00:00:40.073
-Well, if you do a movie,
you're not going to school.

00:00:40.073 --> 00:00:41.974
So...
-I understand, yeah.

00:00:41.974 --> 00:00:44.577
-I still did it, though.
-That's right.

00:00:44.577 --> 00:00:46.713
Look at you now.
Come on. Yeah, exactly right.

00:00:46.713 --> 00:00:48.647
[ Applause ]

00:00:48.647 --> 00:00:51.216
-So they made me repeat
the year.

00:00:51.216 --> 00:00:52.451
-Oh, really? They did?

00:00:52.451 --> 00:00:53.419
-It was worth it.

00:00:53.419 --> 00:00:54.887
-Yeah. Oh, good. Yeah.

00:00:54.887 --> 00:00:58.324
I also heard something that you
used to hitchhike to school.

00:00:58.324 --> 00:00:59.725
-Yeah. Didn't you?

00:00:59.725 --> 00:01:01.694
-No. No. That's very dangerous.

00:01:01.694 --> 00:01:02.661
I don't hitchhike.

00:01:02.661 --> 00:01:04.129
-No, it's not in Cuba.

00:01:04.129 --> 00:01:07.967
I mean, you just get there
faster than just --

00:01:07.967 --> 00:01:09.435
-I understand, yeah, but...

00:01:09.435 --> 00:01:10.803
-I will get there faster
than you, maybe.

00:01:10.803 --> 00:01:11.871
-Yes, you will. Yeah.

00:01:11.871 --> 00:01:13.206
Because no one
would pick me up.

00:01:13.206 --> 00:01:15.641
If we're both on the street
with our thumb out,

00:01:15.641 --> 00:01:17.077
they're gonna pick you up
and not me.

00:01:17.077 --> 00:01:18.444
-Well, I didn't
do the thumb thing.

00:01:18.444 --> 00:01:21.781
I'd just go to the stoplight,
so the cars have to stop.

00:01:21.781 --> 00:01:23.449
-You would just jump into
strangers' cars,

00:01:23.449 --> 00:01:24.851
like, "Take me to school"?

00:01:24.851 --> 00:01:26.386
-Pretty much.
-Yeah?

00:01:26.386 --> 00:01:27.820
-You just go to the window.

00:01:27.820 --> 00:01:29.856
I'm like, "Hey, can you go
to the next stoplight?"

00:01:29.856 --> 00:01:32.825
-No, this is too dangerous.
Oh no, no.

00:01:32.825 --> 00:01:34.727
-No, it's not. I mean,
everyone's very used to it.

00:01:34.727 --> 00:01:39.098
It's like free carpool.

00:01:39.098 --> 00:01:43.236
-Any children watching,
don't do this.

00:01:43.236 --> 00:01:47.707
But is that how you
ended up in the Bond movie?

00:01:47.707 --> 00:01:49.509
Because you're from --
No, no, no! Not hitchhiking.

00:01:49.509 --> 00:01:50.843
Not hitchhiking.

00:01:50.843 --> 00:01:52.178
Being from Cuba, sorry.
-"Hey."

00:01:52.178 --> 00:01:53.880
"Hi, do you guys mind
if I'm in this movie?"

00:01:53.880 --> 00:01:55.648
-"Do you go to London?"

00:01:55.648 --> 00:01:57.984
-"Can I be in the new
007 movie?"

00:01:57.984 --> 00:01:59.219
"Sure. Come on."

00:01:59.219 --> 00:02:01.020
No, but is it
because you're from Cuba?

00:02:01.020 --> 00:02:03.622
Is that how?

00:02:03.622 --> 00:02:06.458
-I mean, something
to do with that.

00:02:06.458 --> 00:02:08.528
I think...

00:02:08.528 --> 00:02:09.862
-You're so good in this,
by the way.

00:02:09.862 --> 00:02:11.764
I told you backstage,
but I really mean it.

00:02:11.764 --> 00:02:13.700
-Thank you.
-You get a giant laugh.

00:02:13.700 --> 00:02:15.134
I'm not going to spoil
anything for anyone.

00:02:15.134 --> 00:02:17.837
I won't ever do that.
but dude.

00:02:17.837 --> 00:02:20.706
This one scene,
it's just beautiful to look at.

00:02:20.706 --> 00:02:22.474
I go, it's it's iconic,

00:02:22.474 --> 00:02:23.543
It's iconic.
-Thank you.

00:02:23.543 --> 00:02:24.476
-You did, you crushed it.
You're fantastic.

00:02:24.476 --> 00:02:25.945
-Thank you. Thank you.

00:02:25.945 --> 00:02:28.948
-Do you want to describe
who you play? Your 00 agent?

00:02:28.948 --> 00:02:33.953
-Yeah, I play Paloma.
She's a CIA agent in Cuba.

00:02:33.953 --> 00:02:38.424
-She's there to assist Bond
in his mission.

00:02:38.424 --> 00:02:41.160
And she very excited
about the job.

00:02:41.160 --> 00:02:44.264
-Yeah, yeah. You really are.
-She's very, very happy,

00:02:44.264 --> 00:02:46.032
and like, you know, also nervous

00:02:46.032 --> 00:02:48.768
because it's her first job,
big, big job.

00:02:48.768 --> 00:02:52.171
-Yeah, you're like --
I could say the line.

00:02:52.171 --> 00:02:53.339
You're like,

00:02:53.339 --> 00:02:54.507
"Oh, I'm only three weeks
in training on the job."

00:02:54.507 --> 00:02:56.876
-Yeah, yeah, exactly.
-Yeah.

00:02:56.876 --> 00:02:58.911
-The funny thing is that
I also had only

00:02:58.911 --> 00:03:03.082
three weeks training,
so I think I just kept saying it

00:03:03.082 --> 00:03:07.487
so much that Cary was like,
"Just say it. It's fine."

00:03:07.487 --> 00:03:10.089
-Oh, because that's real life.
-"Just keep it."

00:03:10.089 --> 00:03:12.391
-You just came from doing
a Marilyn Monroe movie

00:03:12.391 --> 00:03:13.393
right to this.

00:03:13.393 --> 00:03:14.660
-Yeah.

00:03:14.660 --> 00:03:18.464
-Was that difficult to go
from that extreme to this?

00:03:18.464 --> 00:03:21.400
-Yeah. Well...yeah.
-Yeah.

00:03:21.400 --> 00:03:25.137
-I mean,
Marilyn did not train at all.

00:03:25.137 --> 00:03:26.906
-No. Yeah, no.
-Like Paloma.

00:03:26.906 --> 00:03:31.678
I mean, it was, it's like
opposite things, you know?

00:03:31.678 --> 00:03:34.947
I did Marilyn,
it was a very intense,

00:03:34.947 --> 00:03:37.750
and then I finished shooting
on a Friday.

00:03:37.750 --> 00:03:39.352
I got on a plane on a Saturday

00:03:39.352 --> 00:03:41.955
and I started shooting Bond
on Monday.

00:03:41.955 --> 00:03:45.424
So I just remember
being on set like,

00:03:45.424 --> 00:03:48.527
my first scene and I kind of
like started whispering

00:03:48.527 --> 00:03:50.362
and Cary was like, "Mmm.

00:03:50.362 --> 00:03:52.731
No, we're here now."

00:03:52.731 --> 00:03:54.801
"You're in this movie now."
-This movie now.

00:03:54.801 --> 00:03:56.068
-[ As Marilyn Monroe ]
"Happy birthday."

00:03:56.068 --> 00:03:58.604
"No, we're not doing that now.
We're doing this."

00:03:58.604 --> 00:04:01.341
-Kind of.
-We're doing this movie now.

00:04:01.341 --> 00:04:04.043
Daniel Craig.
you guys are great together.

00:04:04.043 --> 00:04:06.545
Is it odd that
you were in "Knives Out"

00:04:06.545 --> 00:04:09.081
and then you're with Bond?

00:04:09.081 --> 00:04:10.883
You guys are
a traveling team now.

00:04:10.883 --> 00:04:13.052
-[ Laughing ]
-You go together.

00:04:13.052 --> 00:04:14.653
-Yeah, that was awesome.

00:04:14.653 --> 00:04:18.390
I mean, "Knives Out,"
it was such a special movie.

00:04:18.390 --> 00:04:19.591
We had so much fun,

00:04:19.591 --> 00:04:22.261
and Daniel and I
were together all the time.

00:04:22.261 --> 00:04:23.496
We were this team.

00:04:23.496 --> 00:04:25.297
But back then,

00:04:25.297 --> 00:04:27.666
only Daniel was talking
about Bond and his training.

00:04:27.666 --> 00:04:29.935
I had no idea what was
going to happen.

00:04:29.935 --> 00:04:30.970
-That you were gonna be in it?
-No, no.

00:04:30.970 --> 00:04:33.038
That happened,
like, four months later.

00:04:33.038 --> 00:04:34.072
-He's phenomenal, man.

00:04:34.072 --> 00:04:36.642
-It was a
very happy coincidence.

00:04:36.642 --> 00:04:38.111
-I loved the movie
top to bottom.

00:04:38.111 --> 00:04:39.511
I'm a big fan of all the movies,

00:04:39.511 --> 00:04:41.781
but this one has everything
you could even think about.

00:04:41.781 --> 00:04:44.016
Action, you know,

00:04:44.016 --> 00:04:46.552
suspense, spy thriller thing,
love story.

00:04:46.552 --> 00:04:47.954
-Humor.
-Humor.

00:04:47.954 --> 00:04:51.624
It's emotional,
but also it's real stunts.

00:04:51.624 --> 00:04:55.060
It's not just like a CGI thing,
which, you know, is fine.

00:04:55.060 --> 00:04:58.297
This is like, real
human beings doing crazy stunts.

00:04:58.297 --> 00:04:59.698
You're like, "What?"

00:04:59.698 --> 00:05:02.068
I've never seen anything like
that one motorcycle thing.

00:05:02.068 --> 00:05:03.102
-It is spectacular, really.

00:05:03.102 --> 00:05:04.603
-It's a movie.

00:05:04.603 --> 00:05:07.373
It's just like, wow, they made
an unbelievable movie.

00:05:07.373 --> 00:05:08.841
-You really like it.
-I loved it.

00:05:08.841 --> 00:05:10.375
I loved it. It was so good.

00:05:10.375 --> 00:05:12.244
I want to show everyone
a clip from the movie.

00:05:12.244 --> 00:05:15.515
Here's Ana de Armas in
"No Time to Die." Take a look.

00:05:16.349 --> 00:05:17.450
[ Gunfire ]

00:05:17.450 --> 00:05:22.755
♪♪

00:05:22.755 --> 00:05:30.529
♪♪

00:05:30.529 --> 00:05:38.304
♪♪

00:05:38.304 --> 00:05:46.078
♪♪

00:05:46.078 --> 00:05:47.947
-Yeah!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:47.947 --> 00:05:49.982
That's what I'm talking about!

00:05:49.982 --> 00:05:52.718
That is what I'm talking about!
That exact scene!

00:05:52.718 --> 00:05:54.921
You're amazing. Ana de Armas!

